==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-au-come across.ogg|Audio (AU)|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|comes across|coming across|came across|come across}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To give an [[appearance]] or [[impression]]; to project a certain [[image]].
#: {{ux|en|A business suit and briefcase help her to '''come across''' as the competent professional she is.}}
# To [[find]], usually by [[accident]].
#: {{ux|en|In the meadow he will '''come across''' a rare flower.}}
# {{lb|en|literally|or|figuratively}} To [[change]] [[sides]]; to ask someone to work for the opposition.
#: {{ux|en|You argued well in court but your firm doesn't pay its lawyers well, so why don't you '''come across''' to ours?}}

